; VERIFIED: Plot one vertical half of the LEFT side of a circle outline (used when the right
; side is off the view): one pixel per step at column byte E with mask B, moving outwards
; with RRC B/INC E, row by row up (CircleRowDirection = 0, DEC H) or down (CircleRowDirection = 1, INC H).  The
; midpoint error term and counters are in the alternate registers (HL', DE', BC'); when C'
; reaches A' the arc continues in the two-sided loop (L_878F/L_87D1).  Character-row
; crossing and clipping go through AdjustRowUpAcrossCell/AdjustRowDownAcrossCell; exits restore SP from CircleSavedStackPointer (abort path)
